## 5. P5 bridge confirmed dead

Reconstructed the exact reviewer scenario from
.swarm/verdicts/P5.1.checker-second.verdict: "H & M" and "A & W" each used
to normalize (via the letterless drop alone, pre-P10) to a 2-token key
({H,M} / {A,W}) that could subset-merge into any unrelated key containing
both bare letters as standalone tokens — reproduced there via
`GroupKeys([Normalize("H & M"), Normalize("H M SUPERSTORE DOWNTOWN")])`
merging. Post-P10: Normalize("H & M") = "H&M" (1 token). The worker's own
TestGroupKeys_AmpersandFusionClosesTwoLetterBrandBridge pins this exact
case against a "H STORE M" bridge candidate and asserts no merge + 2
groups — I re-verified by hand-tracing shouldMerge: "H&M" is a 1-token
(degenerate) key, and the guard (merchants.go:257-261) forces degenerate
keys to merge only on EXACT string equality, never subset containment, so
"H&M" cannot merge into "H STORE M" (3-token) or any other key regardless
of its contents. Also re-verified TestGroupKeys_AmpersandFusedKeysDistinct
AndExactOnly ("A&W" vs "H&M" stay separate) and the end-to-end
TestGroupTransactions_AmpersandSpacedAndUnspacedMerge (spaced "H & M" and
unspaced "H&M 4821" land in one group under canonical key "H&M") — all
pass. The P5 bridge is genuinely closed, not just reduced.

